# ShortForge API keys — copy this file to ".env" and fill in your own keys.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # then edit .env
#
# ShortForge loads ./.env automatically on every run (see --env-file to point
# elsewhere). Real shell environment variables always take precedence, so an
# `export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...` in your shell overrides this file.
#
# ".env" is git-ignored — your keys stay on your machine and are never
# committed or sent anywhere except to the API you configured.
#
# EVERYTHING BELOW IS OPTIONAL. With no keys at all, ShortForge still runs fully
# offline: heuristic hook detection, offline Argos translation, espeak TTS.

# --- LLM provider (Part E) ---------------------------------------------------
# Enables smarter hook detection, higher-quality translation, and SEO metadata.
# Works with Anthropic directly OR any OpenAI-compatible gateway (many third-party
# providers serve Claude- and GPT-family models at their own base URL).
#
#   LLM_PROVIDER = anthropic | openai | none
#   LLM_BASE_URL = the gateway's base URL (find it in your provider's API docs;
#                  OpenAI-style usually ends in /v1). Leave blank for the vendor default.
#   LLM_API_KEY  = your key for that provider
#   LLM_MODEL    = the model id to use (e.g. claude-opus-4-8, gpt-4o-mini)
#
# Test it with:  python cli.py check-llm
LLM_PROVIDER=
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=

# Back-compat: if you use Anthropic directly you can just set this instead of the
# LLM_* block above (ShortForge falls back to it automatically).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
